<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91245" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύγμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fold</i> or <i>anything
			folded</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλοιο π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.315
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.271
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phaedim.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοῦ δέρματος</span>
			<i>fold</i> of skin, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.15.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὑστέρας</span>, =
			<i>fundus</i> uteri, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.64
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Medic.,
				<i>piece of lint folded up to stop a wound, pledget</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.13.27
			</span></i>; of a bandage, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).826
			</span></i>.</div>
